### Shopping List API — full workflow
###
### Runnable from Visual Studio, Rider, or VS Code (REST Client extension).
### Committed to the repository rather than shared as a Postman export, so it is versioned
### alongside the endpoints it exercises and cannot drift unnoticed.
###
### Run top to bottom: the token, item id and image id flow between requests automatically.

@host = http://localhost:5080
@keycloak = http://localhost:8080

@username = demo
@password = DemoPassw0rd!

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 1. Signup — creates a user in Keycloak via a scoped service account.
### The password is forwarded to the identity provider and never stored by this API.
### Expect 409 if you run this twice.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "reviewer",
  "email": "reviewer@example.com",
  "firstName": "Alex",
  "lastName": "Reviewer",
  "password": "ReviewerPassw0rd!"
}

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 2. Token — OAuth2 Direct Access Grant.
### DEPRECATED in OAuth 2.1; present so the API can be driven from the command line.
### Authorization Code + PKCE is enabled on the same client (see request 14).
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# @name token
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{username}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

@accessToken = {{token.response.body.accessToken}}
@refreshToken = {{token.response.body.refreshToken}}

### 3. Refresh — the realm rotates refresh tokens and rejects reuse.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 4. Create an item. Embedding is generated asynchronously — the response returns
### immediately with embeddingStatus "Pending".
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# @name createItem
POST {{host}}/api/v1/items
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Organic whole milk",
  "notes": "2 litre bottle, semi-skimmed is an acceptable substitute",
  "quantity": 2,
  "unit": "bottle",
  "category": "dairy"
}

@itemId = {{createItem.response.body.id}}

### 5. A few more items, so search has something to rank.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/items
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Washing up liquid", "notes": "lemon scented, for dishes", "quantity": 1, "unit": "bottle", "category": "household" }

###
POST {{host}}/api/v1/items
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Mature cheddar cheese", "notes": "block, not grated", "quantity": 1, "unit": "block", "category": "dairy" }

###
POST {{host}}/api/v1/items
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Wholemeal bread", "notes": "seeded loaf", "quantity": 1, "unit": "loaf", "category": "bakery" }

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 6. Read back. Poll until embeddingStatus is "Ready" before running the semantic
### search below — until then the vector branch has nothing to match against.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
GET {{host}}/api/v1/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 7. List with keyset pagination and metadata filters.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/items?pageSize=10&category=dairy
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 8. Hybrid search — keyword match. Both branches contribute; check vectorRank
### and textRank in the response to see which found what.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
POST {{host}}/api/v1/search
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "milk", "limit": 10 }

### 9. Semantic match — no shared keyword with the item.
### "dish soap" should surface "Washing up liquid" through the vector branch alone.
### This is the result an INNER JOIN between the branches would have discarded.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/search
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "dish soap", "limit": 10 }

### 10. Hybrid with metadata filters — pushed into both retrieval branches, not
### applied after fusion.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/search
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "cheese", "category": "dairy", "isPurchased": false, "limit": 10 }

### 11. Malformed query. websearch_to_tsquery tolerates this; to_tsquery would
### raise a syntax error and return 500.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/search
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "milk & \"unclosed", "limit": 10 }

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 12. Update. Changing name or notes clears the embedding and re-queues the item,
### so it cannot keep matching its old description.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
PUT {{host}}/api/v1/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Organic semi-skimmed milk",
  "notes": "4 pint bottle",
  "quantity": 1,
  "unit": "bottle",
  "category": "dairy",
  "isPurchased": true
}

### 13. Image upload. Content type is determined from the file's magic bytes, not
### the Content-Type header or the extension. Replace the path with a real image.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/items/{{itemId}}/images
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary

--boundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="photo.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./photo.png
--boundary--

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 14. Authorization Code + PKCE — the intended production flow.
### Open in a browser; request 2 exists only for command-line convenience.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# {{keycloak}}/realms/shopping-list/protocol/openid-connect/auth
#   ?client_id=shopping-list-api
#   &response_type=code
#   &scope=openid profile email
#   &redirect_uri=http://localhost:5080/
#   &code_challenge=<S256 challenge>
#   &code_challenge_method=S256

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Negative cases — these SHOULD fail. Each proves a control is working.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 15. No token → 401. Proves the fallback authorization policy fails closed.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/items

### 16. Cross-user access → 404, not 403.
### Get a token as demo2 (password DemoPassw0rd!) and request demo's item id.
### 404 rather than 403 is deliberate: 403 would confirm the id exists.
GET {{host}}/api/v1/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer PASTE_A_DEMO2_TOKEN_HERE

### 17. Validation failure → 400 with per-field errors as problem+json.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/items
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "", "quantity": -5 }

### 18. Oversized search query → 400. Bounded because the query is embedded,
### and an unbounded string is an unbounded inference cost.
POST {{host}}/api/v1/search
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "" }

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Operations
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 19. Liveness — checks nothing external, so a dependency outage cannot cause
### the orchestrator to restart healthy replicas.
GET {{host}}/health/live

### 20. Readiness — per-dependency detail. Redis and Ollama report Degraded rather
### than Unhealthy: the API serves without them.
GET {{host}}/health/ready

### 21. Prometheus metrics.
GET {{host}}/metrics

### 22. Delete. Removes the item, its image rows, and the stored objects.
DELETE {{host}}/api/v1/items/{{itemId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
